From: thingino sigmastar port
Subject: [PATCH] assembly.h: use the portable C path on ARM

assembly.h picks an implementation of MULSHIFT32/FASTABS/CLZ per platform and
ends in "#error Unsupported platform in assembly.h". Both ARM branches are
disabled upstream by deliberately misspelt guards:

    #elif defined (XXX__arm) && defined (__ARMCC_VERSION)
    #elif defined(__GNUC__) && defined(XXXX__arm__)

so an ARM GCC build matches nothing and hits the #error. The portable C branch
just below covers ARDUINO, mips, powerpc and Solaris but not arm.

This is not a compile-time failure in practice, which is what makes it nasty.
libhelix-aac.mk compiles the sources with a $(foreach ...) loop whose commands
are joined by ";", so a file that fails to compile does not stop the loop, and
the final link is "-shared" over whatever .o files exist -- which permits
undefined symbols. The result on ARM was 13 objects out of 28 sources and a
libhelix-aac.so that loads and then dies on first use:

    rwd: symbol lookup error: /lib/libhelix-aac.so: undefined symbol: UncoupleSBRNoise

(UncoupleSBRNoise lives in sbrhuff.c, one of the 15 that never compiled. All 15
include assembly.h; the 13 that built do not.)

Add __arm__/__aarch64__ to the portable branch. That is exactly the path MIPS
already takes, so this is the code thingino has been shipping on Ingenic all
along -- plain C, no inline assembly, no new risk. Reviving the disabled ARM
assembly branch would be the other option, but it is disabled upstream for a
reason nobody has written down, and correctness beats a guess at speed for an
AAC decoder used by the WebRTC audio path.

--- a/src/libhelix-aac/assembly.h
+++ b/src/libhelix-aac/assembly.h
@@ -533,7 +533,7 @@ static __inline Word64 MADD64(Word64 sum64, int x, int y) {
     return sum64;
 }
 
-#elif defined(ARDUINO) || defined(__GNUC__) && (defined(__mips__) || defined(__MIPS__)) || defined(__GNUC__) && (defined(__powerpc__) || defined(__POWERPC__)) || (defined (_SOLARIS) && !defined (__GNUC__) && !defined (_SOLARISX86))
+#elif defined(ARDUINO) || defined(__GNUC__) && (defined(__mips__) || defined(__MIPS__)) || defined(__GNUC__) && (defined(__arm__) || defined(__aarch64__)) || defined(__GNUC__) && (defined(__powerpc__) || defined(__POWERPC__)) || (defined (_SOLARIS) && !defined (__GNUC__) && !defined (_SOLARISX86))
 
 typedef long long Word64;
 
